The genealogy of Jesus' family.
This is the hospital of the lineage of Sayyidina Isa ibn Maryam. He is the son of Sayyidina Dawud. And he is also the son of Sayyidina Ibrahim.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah the father of Perez and Zerah, and their mother was Tamar. Perez was the father of Hezron. And Hezron was the father of Aram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Boaz was the father of Obed. Rahab was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. Solomon's mother was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa was the son of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the son of Joram. Joram was the son of Uzziah.
Uzziah was the father of Jotham. Jotham was the father of Ahaz. Ahaz was the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jehoiakim and his brothers. In those days, the Jewish people were forced to leave for Babylon.
And after this thing, the family series continued. Jekoniah was the father of Shallum. Shallum was the father of Zebedee.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Aaim. Aaim was the father of Elmodad.
Eliud was the father of Eliezer. Eliezer was the father of Mathan. Mathan was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
There were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David until the Jews were forced to go to Babylon. And there were 14 from that time to Christ. Jesus Christ was born.
Thus was the birth of Jesus Christ. His mother Mary and his brother Joseph were married, but before they began to live together, it appeared to them that she would give birth. She conceived by the Holy Spirit.
Her husband Joseph was a good man. He didn't want to expose her to the public. That's why he planned to divorce her in secret.
But suddenly, Jawad, and how he was thinking about this, an angel appeared to him from God in a dream. The angel said to him, "O Jawad, son of David, fear not, but take Mary into your house and make her your wife. This child that is in her womb is from the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a son. You must name him Jesus. This is because he will save his people from their sins.
All this was done so that it would be as my Lord said, it will be. He said with the tongue of the Prophet,
The virgin will be with child. She will be with child and give birth to a son. And they will name him Emmanuel.
Joseph woke up. He realized that the angel of the Lord had told him. He took her to his house to his wife Mary.
But she didn't want to love her even after she gave birth to a son. And our Lord Joseph called him Jesus.
The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This took place during the time when Herod was king over Judea. After Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
"Then they said to him, 'Where is the child who has been born to be king of the Jews? For we have seen his star in the east and have come to worship him.'"
When King Herod heard this news, he became very angry. Indeed, all the people in Jerusalem were disturbed.
Herod called together all the chief priests of the people, as well as the teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah would be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they replied. "For this is what is written by the prophet: 'And you, Bethlehem, in the land of Judah, are by no means least among the rulers of Judah; for out of you will come a ruler who will shepherd my people Israel.'"
"And you, Bethlehem, land of Judah, what are you among the clans of Judah? From you will come for me the one who will be ruler, and he will be shepherd of my people Israel."
That's why Herod called for the wise men in secret. He knew exactly where they had seen the star.
I sent them to Bethlehem. He said to them, "Go! Search diligently for that child. And when you find him, bring me word, so that I too may go and pay him homage."
And after they heard the king, they took their way. That star which they saw in the east went before them. And when they had come to the end of their journey, they found the place where the child was.
And when they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men went home. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They bowed down to him and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense and myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. And they returned to their country by another way. Jesus's family fled to Egypt.
When the men went to the fair, Joseph dreamed a dream. In the dream, an angel of God appeared to him. "Arise!" the angel said to him. "Take the child and his mother and flee into Egypt. Stay there until I bring you back. Herod is going to search for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph got up. At night, he went to Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They remained there until King Herod died. In this way, the words spoken by the Lord through the prophet were fulfilled. He had said, "I have decided to bring my son out of Egypt." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod was told by the wise men that the priests had deceived him. And he remained very angry. And he ordered the killing of all the boys who were in Bethlehem and the surrounding area, who were aged from two years upwards, according to the time which they had ascertained from the appearance of the stars. This was the fulfilment of what was spoken by the prophet, 'A voice in Ramah, lamentation and great weeping, Ramah is mourning for her children, as they are slain in the presence of their mother, with the sword of the enemy, who has no pity upon the children, for these are the days of vengeance, to fulfil that which is spoken by the prophet, "The breath of the Lord, like a stream of brimstone, sets ablaze the forest, and the mountain top is scorched." '
Thus, the words of the prophet Jeremiah were fulfilled. He had said,
It sounds like a voice in Ramah. That is the sound of weeping and deep sorrow. Rachel is weeping for her children. She does not want anyone to comfort her, because her children are dead.
And after Herod died, Joseph dreamed while he was still staying in Egypt. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him.
The angel said to him, "Rise! Take the child and his mother. Go to the land of Israel. Those who were trying to kill the child are dead."
Joseph stood up and took the boy and his mother Mary back with them to the land of Israel.
But after he heard that Archelaus had become king of Judea - Archelaus was the one who was ruling in place of his father Herod - this made Joseph afraid to return. So in a dream, Joseph got up and returned to the land of Galilee.
He lived there in a country called Nazareth. In this way, the prophecies of the prophets about Jesus were fulfilled. They prophesied that he would be called the Nazarene.
John the Baptist is paving the way.
So you waited for the right moment, and here comes John the Baptist, and he starts preaching in the Judean desert.
He said, "Turn away from your sins! The Kingdom of Heaven is near."
John is the one who prepared the way for Him, to whom the Prophets Isaiah spoke. He said, "Is there anyone among men who is trying to call out in the wilderness, saying, 'Here is the place where the Lord will pass through the wilderness of the peoples. You should prepare the way for Him and make His paths straight.' " (Isaiah 40:3)
John's clothes were made from camel hair. He was wearing a leather belt at his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.
The people were driven out of Jerusalem and all areas of Judea, and even from the areas along the Jordan River.
From where they confessed their sins, John baptized them in the Jordan Valley.
John saw many Pharisees and Sadducees coming to the place where he was baptizing. He said to them, "You are like a brood of vipers! Who warned you to flee from the coming wrath of God?"
Produce fruits that show you have repented of your sins.
Don't worry about suggesting this idea: "Abraham is our father." I'm telling you, God is capable of giving Abraham children even from this very stone.
The axe is right under the roots of the trees. Every tree that does not bear good fruit will be cut down. It will be burned with fire.
"I baptize you with water, and I advise you to repent of your sins. But after me, one will come who is stronger than I am. And I am not worthy to carry his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire."
He makes the water mill turn with his hand in order to grind the straw from the house. He will gather his wheat for the granary. But he will burn the chaff with the unquenchable fire."
Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan River. He wanted to be baptized by John.
But John tried to prevent him. He said to him, "I need to be baptized by you. Why are you coming to me?"
Jesus answered, "Let it be so now. It is proper for us to do this. They are carrying out the holy plan of God." John agreed.
As soon as Jesus was baptized, he went up out of the water. At that moment, the heavens were opened to him. He saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and coming to rest on him.
I heard a voice from heaven, saying, "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased."
Jesus is tempted.
The Holy Spirit led Jesus into the desert. There the devil tempted him.
And after forty days and nights without eating, Jesus was hungry.
Jahweh said to the devil, "If you are the son of God, command these stones to become bread."
Jesus answered and said, "It is written in the Quran: 'No human lives by bread alone, but by every word that comes from the mouth of God.' (Deuteronomy 8:3)"
And the Devil took Jesus up to a very high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms of the world in an instant. And he said to him, 'All this I will give you if you fall down and worship me.'
He said to him: "If you are the Son of God, command that these stones become bread. For it is written: 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3, Matthew 4:1-4)
Jesus answered them, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone.' " (Deuteronomy 6:16)
In the end, the Devil took Saeed to a very high mountain. And there, all of them were from the kingdoms of the world and their splendor.
He told them, "If you prostrate yourselves to me and worship me, I will give you all of this."
Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written: 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only' " (Deuteronomy 6:13)
And what a great victory Satan had over Jesus. They came to him with the angels and took him by his head. Jesus began to preach and give sermons.
John was in prison. When Jesus heard about this, he returned to Galilee.
Jesus left Nazareth. He went and lived in the town of Capernaum. Which is on the shore of the lake in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali.
Thus it was, that what Isaiah the prophet had said was fulfilled.
Land of Zebulun! Land of Naphtali! Galilee, where non-Jews live! Land on the coast of the Mediterranean Sea! Territory east of the Jordan River!
The people who live in the land of deep darkness will see a great light. They live now in a land of deep darkness, but the light will shine upon them.
From that time on, Jesus began to preach to the people. "Repent of your sins!" he said. "For the Kingdom of Heaven is at hand." Jesus chose his first disciples.
One day Jesus was walking by the Sea of Galilee. There he saw two brothers. They were Simon Peter and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the lake. They were fishermen.
Come, follow me, said Jesus. "I will make you fishers of men."
Immediately, they left their nets and followed him.
Having walked a little further, he saw two other brothers. They were James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. They were in the boat with their father Zebedee. As they were mending their nets, Jesus called out to them.
Immediately they left the boat and their father, and followed Jesus. Jesus healed the sick people.
Jesus went throughout Galilee. There he taught in the synagogues. He preached the grace of the Kingdom of God. And he healed all the diseases and ills of the people.
The news spread about him throughout all of Syria. People brought to him all who were sick with various diseases. There were some who were suffering from great pains. And there were some who were possessed by demons. There were some who were shaking violently. And there were some who were unable to move at all. And Jesus healed them all.
Large crowds were following him. People came from Galilee, from the region that is called Decapolis, and from Jerusalem and Judea. And other people came from the region across the Sea of Galilee, which is the region of the Gerasenes.
Jesus performs miracles.
Jesus saw the crowds. He went up on a mountain and sat down. His disciples came to him.
And he began to teach them. He said,
Blessed are those who are spiritually needy. The Kingdom of Heaven will be theirs.
Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted.
Blessed are the meek, for they shall inherit the earth.
Blessed are those who wait for the right and thirst for it. They will be satisfied.
Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy.
Blessed are the pure in heart. They will see God.
Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God.
Blessed are those who are tormented when they do what is right. Their paradise is here.
Blessed are you when people mock and harm you because of me. And blessed are you also when they fabricate all kinds of malicious lies because of me.
Be happy and pleased. Your reward in Paradise is great. This is like what people used to do with the prophets before. Salt and light.
You are the salt of the earth. But if the salt loses its saltiness, how can it be made salty again? It is no longer good for anything, but will be thrown out and trampled underfoot.
You are the light of the world. No one can hide a city on a hill.
Also, people don't usually put a candle under a bowl. They put it on top of its stand. That way, the light shines for everyone in the house.
In the same way, let my light shine before people. In this way, they will see the good things you do. And they will praise your great leader in heaven. Jesus gives complete meaning to the law.
Do not reproduce, I came to cancel what is written in the Torah or in the Prophets. I did not come to do this. I came to give the true meaning of what is written.
What I am going to tell you is true. Heaven and earth will pass away before even one stroke of any letter from the Law is annihilated. Not even a dot from a pen will be removed from the Law until everything is completed.
Do not break even one of the least commandments. And do not teach people to break them. Because you will remain known as the least people in the Kingdom of Heaven. Instead, practice these commandments and teach them to people. This is how you will remain known as important people in the Kingdom of Heaven.
This is what I'm telling you. You need to be more righteous than the Pharisees and teachers of the law. Otherwise, you will not enter the kingdom of heaven. Murder.
Have you heard what they did to the people who were in the ancient times? They said to them, "You shall not kill. (Exodus 20:13) Whoever kills will be held accountable for his action."
But that's what I'm going to tell you. Don't be angry with your brother. Whoever is angry with his brother will be subject to judgment. Once again, whoever says to his brother, "You fool!" will be subject to the Sanhedrin court. But whoever says to him, "You moron!" will be in danger of the fires of hell.
You imagine now that you are presenting your gift at the altar. And you think that your brother has something on you.
Leave your gift in front of the altar. First, go and be reconciled with your brother, and then come and offer your gift.
We think someone has a claim against you and will drag you to court. Try to resolve the issue quickly. Do it before you part ways. Because if you don't, he will drag you to the judge. And the judge will drag you to the police. And they might take you to prison.
What I'm going to tell you is true. You're not leaving until you pay the last cent! The whore.
Have you not heard that it was said, "Do not commit adultery"? (Exodus 20:14)
But this is what I will tell you. Don't look at women in the wrong way. The one who does this commits adultery with her in his heart.
If your right eye causes you to sin, pluck it out and throw it away. For your eye is only a single part of your body. It is better for you to lose that one part of your body than for your entire body to be thrown into hell.
"If your right hand is causing you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. Your hand is just a part of your body. It is better to lose it than to throw your whole body into hell. Divorce."
It was said, 'If a man divorces his wife, he must give her a certificate of divorce.' (Deuteronomy 24:1)
But this is what I will tell you. Whoever divorces his wife leaves her to commit adultery. And whoever marries a divorced woman commits adultery. A man can only divorce his wife if she commits adultery against him. The oath.
Once again, you have heard what was said to your people long ago. They were told, 'Do not break the covenants you make with the Lord. Keep the oaths you have sworn to him.'
But this is what I will tell you. Do not make such a promise. Do not promise it in the name of God. This is God's throne.
Do not name them after the earth. That is the seat of God's feet. Do not name them after Jerusalem. This is the city of the great King.
And what you swore by your heads, God does not hear from you, and He does not hear, and what you swore by your heads, God does not hear from you, and He does not hear.
Let your yes be yes, and your no be no. Anything else comes from the devil. Be kind to people.
Have you heard what they were saying? "An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth." (Exodus 21:24; Leviticus 24:20; Deuteronomy 19:21)
But this is what I'm telling you. Don't fight with someone who is bad."If someone strikes you on your right cheek, give him your left cheek."
If someone brings you to court to take your shirt from you, give him even your jacket.
If someone you are going to leave behind can only walk a mile, go two miles with them.
Give to those who ask something of you. Do not offer to those who want to show something of you. Love your enemy.
Did you hear what he was saying: "Love your neighbor. (Leviticus 19:18) And hate your enemy."
But this is what I will tell you. Love your enemies. Pray for those who hurt you.
And then you will be sons of your Father in heaven. "He makes his sun shine on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the just and the unjust."
If you love those who love you, what will you do? Even tax collectors do that.
If you only greet your own people, what are you doing more than other people? Even those who have no religion do this.
Be perfect, just as your heavenly Father is perfect.
Giving to those in need.
Beware of doing "good works" before people. Do not do them so that people can see you. Because if you do that, your father in heaven will not consider you for doing this.
When you give to those in need, do not blow a trumpet before you. Do not be like those hypocrites who make a show of their piety. They build grand monuments to their own generosity, both inside synagogues and out in public squares. They love to be honored by the people. What I am telling you is the truth. The desires they pursue will never satisfy them.
When you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing.
And after that, you will give your charity in secret. And your Father will reward you. He is the one who sees what you do in secret. Prayer.
When you pray, don't be like the hypocrites. They love to stand and pray in the synagogues and at street corners. They want people to see them. What I tell you is true. The things they are given, they take.
"When you pray, go into your room. Close the door and pray to your father who cannot be seen. He will reward you. Your father sees what is done in secret."
"When you pray, do not babble on like some people who have no religion. They think they will be heard for their much speaking."
Don't be like them. Your father knows what you need before you ask him.
This is how you pray: "Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name."
Your realm is realized. Just as you wish it to be, may it be on earth as it is in heaven.
Give us our daily bread.
Overlook our sins, just as we have forgiven those who have sinned against us.
He kept us from sinning when we are tempted. He delivered us from the evil one.
Forgive people who have wronged you. That will make your father in heaven forgive you.
But if you don't allow people to forgive their sins, your father will still not forgive your sins. Fasting.
"When you don't eat, you're not like those who pretend to be holy. They make their faces sour. They want people to see that they are fasting. What I am telling you is true. What they will take completely."
But when you go away without eating, put oil on your head. Wash your face.
Even if people are around, they won't know that you are fasting, only your father who doesn't see it will know. He will reward you. Your father sees what you do in secret. Hide your wealth in Paradise.
Do not accumulate your wealth only in this world. Swine and rust consume it, and thieves enter and steal it.
Store your wealth in the sky, for there are no worms or rust to spoil it, and no thieves to break in.
Your heart will be where your treasure is.
The eye is like a light that gives light to the body. Imagine if your eyes were beautiful, your whole body would be shining.
But imagine if your eyes were bad. Then your whole body would be in darkness. If the light within you is darkness, then the darkness is pitch black!
There is no one who will serve two masters at the same time. They will hate one and love the other, or they will be loyal to one and hate the other. You cannot serve both God and money at the same time. Fear not.
I tell you, don't worry about yourselves. Don't worry about your life and what you will eat or drink. And don't worry about your body and what you will wear. Is life just eating? Is the body just clothing?
Look at the birds of the sky; for they neither sow nor reap nor gather into barns. But your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not of more value than they?
Will you add an hour to your life by worrying?
And why do you worry about clothing? Look at how flowers grow in nature. They don't get tired or sew clothes.
But this is what I will tell you. Even Solomon at the height of his glory was not dressed like these flowers.
If this is how God takes care of a little grass in the forest, He will take care of you much better than this? The grass will only last one day, tomorrow it will be in the fire. Your faith is too weak!"
Don't be afraid. Don't worry. Don't ask, "What will we eat?" or "What will we drink?" or "What will we wear?"
People without religion run after all these things. Your Father who is in heaven knows that you need all these things.
But seek first the kingdom of God. Do His will. Then all these things will be given to you as well.
Don't worry about tomorrow, tomorrow will worry about itself. Each day has enough worries of its own.
Be fair when you judge people.
Don't judge people. You will be judged.
You will be judged by the same standard you judge others. You will be measured by the same measure you measure others.
You see only the straw in your friend's eye, but the beam in your own eye you do not notice.
You can tell your friends, "Let me get some of that sawdust out of your eye." And you have a log in your own eye?
What a load of hypocrisy! Just look at the log in your own eye before you start worrying about the speck in your friend's eye!
Do not give what is sacred to the dogs. Do not throw your pearls to the pigs. Because they will trample them underfoot. And then they will come back to bite you. Ask, seek, knock on the door.
Soul, they will give you. Turn, you will find. Knock on the door, they will open it for you.
Everyone who asks will receive. Whoever seeks will find. The door will be opened for those who knock.
Is there anyone among you who would give their child a stone if they asked for bread?
Who among you would give him a snake?
And if you are a demon, you know how to give good gifts to your children. So how will your heavenly Father not give good gifts to those who ask Him!
In everything, do to others what you would have them do to you. This is what is written in the Law and the Prophets. The major and minor gates
Enter the Kingdom of God through the narrow gate. The gate is wide and the road is broad that leads to death and to fire. Many people go this way.
But the gate is narrow and the road is narrow leading to life. Few people find it. The tree and its fruits.
Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.
Do you know what they are really like, from their actions? "When someone comes to cut the grapes from the thorns, does he come to cut the figs from the briers?"
