There are no good fruits on a bad tree.
Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down. And thrown into the fire.
You know a tree by its fruits.
No one will enter the Kingdom of Heaven except the one who told me, "Lord, Lord," but the one who will enter is the one who does the will of God in heaven.
On that day, many people will say to me, "Lord! Lord! Have we not prophesied in your name? Have we not cast out demons in your name? Have we not done many miracles in your name?"
I will tell them clearly: "I don't know you, oh people of the land. Stay away from me, oh companions of evil!" An edifying maxim for the wise and the ignorant.
Well then, everyone who listens to my words and puts them into practice is like the wise man who built his house on the rock.
Kids playing in the rain. The water level rises. The wind blows and hits that house. But she doesn't want to believe it. It's built on sand.
But everyone who hears my words and does not do them is like a foolish man who built his house on the sand.
You smell the rain. You raise the water. You feel the smell and the cold in that house. And at that time, the gold was very, very expensive.
Jesus said all these things. The people were amazed at his teaching.
He used to study like someone who has authority. He does not speak like a teacher of Islamic law.
Jesus heals a man who had a skin disease.
Jesus came down from the mountain. A great crowd followed him.
A man who had a skin disease came and knelt before Jesus. "Lord," he said, "if you are willing, you can make me clean."
Jesus stretched out His hand and touched the man. "I am willing to help you," He said. "Be 'clean'!" As soon as He said this, the man was healed of his skin disease.
Jesus said to him, "Do not tell anyone. Go, show yourself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded." The faith of a leader for the Roman soldiers.
And when Jesus entered Capernaum, a centurion came to him, entreating him,
He said to him, "Sir, your servant is sick at home and cannot move. He is suffering greatly."
Jesus said, "I will go and heal him."
The captain replied, "Sir, I am not worthy of you to come under my roof. But just say the word, and your servant will be healed."
I am a man of high status. I have soldiers who follow me. I tell someone, "Go", and they go. I tell someone, "Come", and they come. I tell my servant, "Tell so-and-so this", and they do.
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed. He said to those who were following him, "Truly I tell you, in all of Israel there was no one with faith like that."
I tell you that people will come from the east and the west. They will take their place at the dinner in the kingdom of heaven. They will sit down with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.
But those who think they belong to the kingdom will be thrown out, into the darkness. There they will weep and grind their teeth."
Jesus said to the Roman leader, "Go! It will happen just as you believe it will." And indeed, his servant was healed at that very hour. Jesus healed many people.
When Jesus entered the house of our Lord Peter, he saw his wife. She was lying in bed. She had a fever.
Jesus touched her hand, and the fever left her. She stood up and began to work for him.
When evening came, they brought to him many people possessed by demons. And he cast out the demons with a word, and he healed all who were sick.
Boys, He did it to fulfill what the prophet Isaiah had said. He said, "He bore the suffering that we should have borne. Even though He bore the diseases that we should have borne." (Isaiah 53:4) Jesus continued assigning tasks.
Jesus saw the crowd that was surrounding him. That is why he gave his disciples orders to go to the other side of the Sea of Galilee.
A law professor went to him. He said to him, "Professor, I will follow you wherever you go."
Jesus answered, "Foxes have dens and birds have nests. But the Son of Man has no place to lay his head."
Another follower said to him, "Master, I wish to return and bury my father first."
But our Lord Jesus said to him, "Follow me. Let the dead bury their own dead." Our Lord Jesus calmed the storm.
Jesus entered the boat. His disciples followed him.
Suddenly, a terrible storm came upon the lake. The waves beat against the boat. But Jesus was sleeping.
The students went and woke him up. They said to him, "Master! Save us! We are going to drown!"
Answer: "Your faith is too weak! Why are you so afraid?" Then, Jesus stood up and commanded the wind and the waves to be still. They became calm, and all was still.
The Companions were astonished. They said, "What kind of man is this? Even the winds and the waves obey him!"
Jesus arrived on the other side of the lake, in the region of the Gadarenes. He encountered two men who were possessed by demons. They had come out of the tombs. These men were so savage that no one could travel on that road.
"O Walid Allah, what do you want from us?" they cried. "You came here to punish us before the time of reckoning comes?"
Not far away, there was a large herd of pigs eating.
The demons asked Jesus, "If you drive us out, let us go into that herd of pigs."
Jesus said to them, "Go!" The demons came out of the men and entered the pigs. The entire herd rushed down the steep bank and into the lake. They drowned in the lake.
Those who were tending the pigs fled. They went to the country and reported to the people what had happened. They told the people about what had happened to the men who were controlled by demons.
The whole city came out to meet Jesus. When they saw him, they pleaded with him to leave their region.
