The appearance of Jesus changed.
After six days, Jesus took with him Peter and James and John, the brother of James. He brought them up onto a high mountain. There they were all alone.
Here before them his features changed. His face was radiating like the sun. His clothing became white like the light.
Suddenly, Moses and Elijah appeared before them. Moses and Elijah were talking with Jesus.
Peter said to Jesus, "Lord, it is better for us to be here. If you wish, I will put up three tents; one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah."
And behold, God sent a bright cloud, and it overshadowed them. And they heard a voice out of the cloud, saying, "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. Listen to him!"
And the disciples said this, and they were struck dumb and fell on their faces to the ground.
But Jesus came and touched them. He said to them, "Get up, and do not be afraid."
And they, looking up into the sky, saw only Jesus.
They went down the mountain. On their way down, Jesus said to them, "Do not look at the things that those who saw saw, and even if you look, do not tell those who are with you. Weep until the Son of Man rises from the dead."
